<h1>Max Solomon</h1>
<p>Treasurer, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026. Party: Republican.</p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Became the Republican nominee by receiving more than 5,000 write-in votes in the March primary after no Republican filed for the office. His campaign emphasizes faith-based public service, accessibility, and direct engagement with voters; he has not published a detailed policy platform for the office that we could find.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Attorney, college political science instructor, and ordained minister from Hazel Crest.</p>
